From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] the idle timeout no longer hands back the launch wake lock

Patch 0046 made the launch wake lock's deadline four times as long, because a
cold start of a large application takes about 17 s on this 996 MHz single core
and the lock was being given up in the middle of every one. The warning stopped
appearing, and the lock went on being released just the same: that patch, and
its comment, had the wrong mechanism.

activityIdleInternalLocked() releases it too. IDLE_TIMEOUT is 10 s and fires
first; it marks the activity idle, allResumedActivitiesIdle() then holds on a
device with one foreground activity, and the lock is handed back 30 s before
the deadline 0046 extended. Test V55 measured a 17.2 s cold start with no
"Launch timeout has expired" line at all, which is what a reader of the log
would have taken for the fix working.

An idle that came from that timeout rather than from the activity itself is not
a finished launch, so it no longer releases the lock. LAUNCH_TIMEOUT_MSG still
bounds how long it can be held. IDLE_TIMEOUT keeps its value and goes on
deciding when activities the system has not heard from are stopped and
destroyed, which is what 512 MB cares about; making that four times as long is
a separate change, and one worth measuring first.

--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/am/ActivityStackSupervisor.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/am/ActivityStackSupervisor.java
@@ -1930,7 +1930,16 @@
                 mService.scheduleAppGcsLocked();
             }
 
-            if (mLaunchingActivity.isHeld()) {
