+            // the launch wake lock back in the middle of every slow start and
+            // undid the longer LAUNCH_TIMEOUT above: a cold start of a large
+            // application takes about 17 s here (Test V51), and the message that
+            // used to say so stopped appearing while the lock was released just
+            // the same (Test V55). LAUNCH_TIMEOUT_MSG still bounds how long it
+            // can be held, and IDLE_TIMEOUT keeps deciding when activities are
